# Responsive UI Rules

## Core Principle
No content may ever overflow, clip, or be hidden. All UI must adapt fluidly to window size.

## Fixed Sizes
- NEVER use `setFixedSize`, `setFixedWidth`, or `setFixedHeight` on content-area widgets.
- Allowed exceptions: sidebar width (260px), avatar button (circle decoration), indicator bars (3px wide).
- For everything else, use `setMinimumSize` + `setMaximumSize` pairs with appropriate `QSizePolicy`.

## Text Overflow
- Every `QLabel` must have EITHER `setWordWrap(True)` OR text elision via `fontMetrics().elidedText()`.
- When eliding, always set `setToolTip(full_text)` so the full text is accessible on hover.
- Badge/chip widgets must have `setMaximumWidth(180)` and elide text that exceeds it.

## Grid Layouts
- Grid column count must be calculated dynamically: `cols = max(1, available_width // (card_width + spacing))`.
- Recalculate on `resizeEvent` (debounced with QTimer, ~50ms).
- Never hardcode column count.

## Scroll Areas
- Every page that can grow vertically must be wrapped in `QScrollArea` with `setWidgetResizable(True)`.
- Horizontal scroll must be disabled (`ScrollBarAlwaysOff`) -- content must reflow instead.
- Exceptions: sidebar (fixed platform count, log panel fills remaining space).

## Two-Column Layouts
- Left columns use `setMinimumWidth` + `setMaximumWidth` (not `setFixedWidth`).
- Right columns use stretch factor `1`.
- Preview images scale via `resizeEvent` using min/max constraints, never fixed pixel sizes.

## Page Transitions
- Use `AnimatedStackedWidget` for all `QStackedWidget` page changes.
- Forward navigation (grid->detail, grid->profile): slide right, 200ms OutCubic.
- Back navigation: slide left, 200ms OutCubic.

## Dialogs
- Dialogs use `setMinimumSize` + `resize()`, never `setFixedSize`.
- Error labels use `setWordWrap(True)` and `adjustSize()` on content change.

## Progress / Status Rows
- Platform name labels: `setMinimumWidth(50)` + `setMaximumWidth(100)` + elide + tooltip.
- Status labels: same min/max pattern + elide + tooltip.
- Progress bar gets stretch factor `1` to fill remaining space.

## Log Panels
- Log panels use `setMinimumHeight(80-100)` with stretch factor, no `setMaximumHeight`.
- They fill available vertical space in their container.
